{% extends "template.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/table/macro.njk" import govukTable %}

{% set pageTitle = "Producer Onboarding - HMCTS API Marketplace - GOV.UK" %}
{% set section = "documentation" %}
{% set breadcrumbs = [
  { text: "Home", href: "/" },
  { text: "Documentation", href: "/documentation" }
] %}

{% block content %}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Producer Onboarding</h1>

    <p class="govuk-body-l">
      Publish your API on the HMCTS API Marketplace so that other teams and partners can find it, try
      it safely, and request access. This page explains what you need before you start, and what
      happens next.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Your API needs all six of these. If one is missing, it is best fixed before onboarding begins.
    </p>

    <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
      <li>A clear description of your API, written as an OpenAPI specification, with sample responses
        &mdash; including what errors look like. Samples must not contain real data.</li>
      <li>Security checks in your API. It checks the security token on every call.</li>
      <li>System-to-system sign-in (OAuth 2.0). Callers are applications, not people logging in.</li>
      <li>Your API is running in each environment we connect to: a test environment with no live data,
        and live.</li>
      <li>Approval to share it with people outside your team.</li>
      <li>A private connection. The marketplace can reach your API privately, agreed with our platform
        team.</li>
    </ol>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Read the <a class="govuk-link" href="/documentation/producer-standards">Producer Guidance</a> page for
      the technical requirements in more detail.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="how-it-fits-together">How it fits together</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Consumers find your API in the catalogue and sign up. Every call goes through our secure
      gateway, which checks who is calling before anything reaches you. While consumers build their
      integration, they use Try It Now: a practice copy of your API that returns your sample
      responses. Once approved, their calls reach your real API.
    </p>

    {# The pub-flow.png diagram from the onboarding content goes here once the image is supplied. #}

    <p class="govuk-body">
      Your API stays with your team. The marketplace adds the catalogue, the security checks and a
      practice sandbox in front of it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="how-onboarding-works">How onboarding works</h2>

    {{ govukTable({
      caption: "Onboarding steps",
      captionClasses: "govuk-visually-hidden",
      firstCellIsHeader: true,
      head: [
        { text: "Step" },
        { text: "What happens" },
        { text: "Who" }
      ],
      rows: [
        [
          { text: "1. Check you are ready" },
          { text: "Go through the list above." },
          { text: "Your team" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "2. Agree the basics" },
          { text: "A short name for your API, which environments, and how we connect to it." },
          { text: "Your team and API Marketplace" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "3. Set up secure access" },
          { text: "We create your API's security identity. Your team sets your API to accept tokens from it." },
          { text: "Your team and API Marketplace" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "4. Connect" },
          { text: "We register your API on our gateway and open the private connection to it." },
          { text: "Your team and API Marketplace" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "5. Build the practice sandbox" },
          { text: "We create Try It Now from your sample responses." },
          { text: "Your team" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "6. List it and test it" },
          { text: "Your API appears in the catalogue, and we test the whole journey together." },
          { text: "Your team and API Marketplace" }
        ],
        [
          { text: "7. Go live" },
          { text: "We release it on the live gateway, then your team publishes the API version." },
          { text: "Your team and API Marketplace" }
        ]
      ]
    }) }}

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="what-you-get">What you get</h2>

    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
      <li>A listing in the API Marketplace catalogue, with your documentation.</li>
      <li>Self-service sign-up, so consumers can register without emailing you.</li>
      <li>Try It Now, so consumers can build and test against sample data before getting real access.</li>
      <li>A secure gateway that checks identity and limits traffic before calls reach you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="get-in-touch">Get in touch</h2>

    <p class="govuk-body">
      To start onboarding, or if you have a question, email the API Marketplace team at
      <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:APIMarketplace@hmcts.net">APIMarketplace@hmcts.net</a>.
    </p>

  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
